@* A lower and an upper bound is two inputs with two names — which is also what a server wants to
   read, so the honest shape and the useful one agree. Radix draws one root with two thumbs and
   posts an array; this posts min and max, and the query string stays readable. *@
<Field Class="w-[420px]">
    <FieldLabel>Price</FieldLabel>
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        <Slider name="min" Min="0" Max="500" Step="10" Value="80" aria-label="Lowest price" />
        <Slider name="max" Min="0" Max="500" Step="10" Value="320" aria-label="Highest price" />
    </div>
    <FieldDescription>Posts as <code>min</code> and <code>max</code>.</FieldDescription>
</Field>
